{
	"_comment": [
		"The shared catalogue of the document key: the internal path out of oc_filecache.path, the share identity of its storage (StorageService::shareIdentities, plan 43-21) and the key both sides must derive from them.",
		"Format 2 (plan 43-22, D-43-15, D-43-17, OE-1 a, OE-5 a), the format the companion hands out: sha256 hex over '2' NUL share NUL share path. With an identity, share is its share and the share path is root '/' path, the path without leading slashes (root empty: the path alone; path empty: the root alone); without an identity share is empty and the share path is the path. The share path is in Unicode NFC like the file cache of Nextcloud, otherwise unchanged: no lower casing of root or path, and the prefix files/ is NOT cut.",
		"Format 1 (plan 43-15) was sha256 hex over the path alone in NFC without leading slashes. Its cases stay as history; only the Python test still recomputes them, the companion no longer derives them.",
		"Every expected value was computed by hand with the command in its derivation field, never with the code under test. A path or root with a decomposed character is hashed in its composed form, so its derivation names the composed spelling. sameAs and differsFrom name another case: by path for format 1, by name for format 2.",
		"php/tests/Unit/DocKeyServiceTest.php reads this file and backend/tests/test_share_identity_cases.py recomputes every key with hashlib; the container never hashes a path itself, it only stores the key it is handed."
	],
	"cases": [
